":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T20:06:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T20:06:08Z","body":"@Nemrosin Normally, shortcuts are retrieved with `ED_GET_SHORTCUT(\"/path/to/shortcut\")`\nBut #54513 changed it so that the freelook camera in the normal editor (see node_3d_editor_plugin.cpp) uses the input map as the editor shortcuts apparently caused some issues. \nSo instead you'd have to call `Input::get_singleton()->is_action_pressed(\"spatial_editor/freelook_forward\")`. The inputs for the freelook camera however are not registered in the context of the debug window (this is the point where my knowledge really goes thin).\n\n Any settings for runtime_node_select.cpp (in 4.6 still included in scene_debugger.cpp) have to be handed over via the `_setup(const Dictionary &p_settings)` `p_settings` parameter, which is called at game_view_plugin.cpp.\n\nI am on vacation right now, but I would try to add the shortcut events to the settings in game_view_plugin.cpp. But perhaps this is also a completely wrong approach.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3880422048/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/393597